# fastpaste pastes by typing Ctrl+V (or Shift+Insert) through a virtual
# keyboard on /dev/uinput. `uaccess` has systemd-logind give the user of
# the active local session read/write access to the device; without it the
# snippet is left on the clipboard for a manual paste instead.
#
# The trade-off: any program that user runs can then type into any window.
# Steam ships the same rule for its controller support.
#
# `static_node` tags /dev/uinput even before the uinput module is loaded,
# on kernels where it is a module rather than built in. The file must sort
# before 73-seat-late.rules, which is where the tag is acted on.
KERNEL=="uinput", SUBSYSTEM=="misc", OPTIONS+="static_node=uinput", TAG+="uaccess"
